": [["/g", -0.5211936235427856], ["/admin", -1.129569172859192]]}, {"t": "pu", "lp": -0.0017245372291654348, "top": [["pu", -0.0017245372291654348], ["fx", -7.30944299697876]]}, {"t": "/", "lp": -0.000423819205025211, "top": [["/", -0.000423819205025211], ["/int", -8.477794647216797]]}, {"t": "xe", "lp": -0.05033387988805771, "top": [["xe", -0.05033387988805771], ["adr", -3.3647470474243164]]}, {"t": ".r", "lp": -0.009756741113960743, "top": [[".r", -0.009756741113960743], [".k", -6.179258823394775]]}, {"t": "st", "lp": -0.0003607923863455653, "top": [["st", -0.0003607923863455653], ["ST", -8.643065452575684]]}, {"t": "`", "lp": -0.000692965229973197, "top": [["`", -0.000692965229973197], ["`,", -9.6184663772583]]}, {"t": " (", "lp": -0.51056307554245, "top": [[" (", -0.51056307554245], [" in", -1.183696985244751]]}, {"t": "or", "lp": -0.09313902258872986, "top": [["or", -0.09313902258872986], ["if", -2.8540966510772705]]}, {"t": " `", "lp": -0.6319848299026489, "top": [[" `", -0.6319848299026489], [" similar", -1.0757313966751099]]}, {"t": "i", "lp": -0.10251786559820175, "top": [["i", -0.10251786559820175], ["intel", -3.152036428451538]]}, {"t": "9", "lp": -3.039883085875772e-05, "top": [["9", -3.039883085875772e-05], ["8", -12.362284660339355]]}, {"t": "1", "lp": -7.510213436034974e-06, "top": [["1", -7.510213436034974e-06], ["xx", -13.627626419067383]]}, {"t": "5", "lp": -7.963497773744166e-05, "top": [["5", -7.963497773744166e-05], ["6", -9.58646297454834]]}, {"t": ".r", "lp": -0.012588427402079105, "top": [[".r", -0.012588427402079105], ["`", -4.579380035400391]]}, {"t": "st", "lp": -0.00011373213055776432, "top": [["st", -0.00011373213055776432], ["`)", -10.534438133239746]]}, {"t": "`", "lp": -0.5318208336830139, "top": [["`", -0.5318208336830139], ["`)", -0.888308048248291]]}, {"t": " on", "lp": -0.5922448039054871, "top": [[" on", -0.5922448039054871], [" for", -1.134275197982788]]}, {"t": " older", "lp": -0.04145998880267143, "top": [[" older", -0.04145998880267143], [" newer", -4.602104187011719]]}, {"t": " setups", "lp": -0.6978493928909302, "top": [[" setups", -0.6978493928909302], [" systems", -1.8846991062164307]]}, {"t": ")", "lp": -0.0016932509606704116, "top": [[")", -0.0016932509606704116], ["),", -6.890653133392334]]}, {"t": " in", "lp": -0.7487877607345581, "top": [[" in", -0.7487877607345581], ["\n", -0.8072860836982727]]}, {"t": " your", "lp": -0.0036024292930960655, "top": [[" your", -0.0036024292930960655], [" the", -5.6761603355407715]]}, {"t": " kernel", "lp": -0.025453263893723488, "top": [[" kernel", -0.025453263893723488], [" Linux", -4.659745693206787]]}], "text": "# CCS Modes on Intel Arc (xe driver)\n\nThe `ccs_mode` parameter controls how Compute Slice (CCS) contexts are distributed across the GPU's compute engines. This is set via the `xe` kernel module parameter (e.g., `modprobe xe ccs_mode=1`).\n\n## The Modes\n\n**ccs_mode 0 (default)**\n- CCS contexts are distributed across **all** CCS engines in a round-robin fashion.\n- This is the standard behavior and works well for most workloads.\n\n**ccs_mode 1**\n- CCS contexts are pinned to a **single CCS engine** for the lifetime of the context.\n- A context binds to one specific compute engine and stays there.\n- This can reduce context-switching overhead and provide more predictable scheduling for workloads that benefit from engine affinity.\n\n**ccs_mode 2**\n- CCS contexts are distributed across CCS engines, but with a **different balancing strategy** than mode 0.\n- Historically this was used to address specific scheduling or load-balancing concerns.\n\n## When to use mode 4\n\nMode 4 is typically used for **debugging and testing** purposes. It's often associated with forcing a specific, deterministic CCS distribution pattern that makes it easier to reproduce or diagnose scheduling issues.\n\n---\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f **Important caveat:** I'm not fully confident in the precise semantics of each numeric mode, as these details can vary between driver versions and aren't always well-documented. The `ccs_mode` parameter has also seen changes over time, and some modes have been added, removed, or repurposed.\n\n**For accurate, current information, I'd recommend:**\n- Checking the kernel documentation: `Documentation/gpu/xe.rst` (or `i915.rst` on older setups) in your kernel"}